{"step_index":277,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-10T13:02:43Z","input_tokens":17573,"cache_read_tokens":211762,"output_tokens":1058,"content":"### Added: Universal Iteration & All-Steps Dry-Run Explorer\n\nYour visualizer now displays the **entire code execution and every iteration at a glance** while keeping the beginner-friendly 3-card teaching view on top.\n\n#### 1. Quick Iteration / Phase Jump Bar (Inside the Teaching Card)\n* Located right at the top of the center **Teaching Area** in [`app_build/index.html`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/index.html).\n* Automatically adapts to **any type of code**:\n  * **Loop Algorithms** (*Kadane's Max Subarray, Binary Search, Two Pointers, Sliding Window*): Shows clickable pills for `⚙️ Setup`, `Iter 1 (i=0)`, `Iter 2 (i=1)`, ..., `🏁 Return / End`.\n  * **OOP / Data Structure Classes** (*`Stack`, `Queue`, `LinkedList`*): Shows clickable pills for `⚙️ Setup`, `1. s = Stack()`, `2. s.push(10)`, `3. s.push(20)`, `4. s.push(30)`, `5. print(s.pop())`, etc.\n  * **Recursive Algorithms** (*Factorial, DFS*): Shows clickable pills for each recursive call (`📞 factorial(k=4)` → `📞 factorial(k=3)` → ... → `🔙 Unwind & Return`).\n* **One-Click Jump**: Click any iteration pill to jump directly to the start of that pass.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Complete Code Iteration & Step-by-Step Dry-Run Panel (Visible Below)\nImplemented in [`app_build/app.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/app.js) (`buildIterationGroups` & `renderArea4AllIterations`) and styled in [`app_build/styles.css`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/styles.css):\n* **Tab 1 — `🔄 Grouped by Iterations / Calls` (Default)**:\n  * Groups all steps into clean **Iteration / Operation Cards**.\n  * Each card header shows the **Iteration Badge**, **Condition / Loop Header**, **End-of-Iteration Variable State** (e.g., `s = Stack(items=[10, 20, 30])` or `c = 4, ans = 4`), and the **Step Range**.\n  * Inside each card, every step in that pass is listed with `Step #`, `Line #`, `Code`, `Plain-English Explanation`, and `Variable Change / Output`.\n* **Tab 2 — `📊 All Steps Table (1 → N)` (Interview Dry-Run Table)**:\n  * Shows every single step from `Step #1` to `Step #N` in a single table (`Step`, `Line`, `Iteration / Phase`, `Scope`, `Code Executed`, `What Happened`, `Variables Snapshot`).\n* **Interactive Synchronization**: Clicking **any step row** in either view immediately updates the Code Editor highlight, the Teaching Card, the Thonny Sub-Expression Evaluator, and the Stack/Heap Memory Visualizer.\n\n---\n\n### Try It Now\nRefresh [`app_build/index.html`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/index.html) (`F5` / `Ctrl+R`) in your browser:\n* Your `class Stack:` code will load with all **9 Phases / 40 Steps** visible in the **Iteration & Dry-Run Explorer** below.\n* Click **`✏️ Paste / Edit Code`** anytime to paste your own code or try the 1-click **Quick DSA Templates** (*Stack OOP*, *Kadane's Max Subarray*, *Binary Search*, *Recursion*).","thinking":"Examining the HTML structure and CSS styles to understand the application's layout and visual presentation. Need to identify how elements are arranged and styled to pinpoint potential areas for improvement or modification. Focusing on understanding how the styles are applied and the resulting impact on the displayed content.\n\n\n"}
