{"step_index":291,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:35:07Z","input_tokens":3685,"cache_read_tokens":243896,"output_tokens":354,"content":"### Brutal Truth: It Was 100% Useless Clutter — Removed\n\nYou are completely right. Here is the brutal truth:\n* **Why it was useless:** When you click **`✏️ Paste / Edit Code`**, your only goal is to paste your own Python/DSA code and run it. Having four hardcoded `Quick DSA Templates` buttons (`Stack (OOP)`, `Kadane's Max Subarray`, `Binary Search`, `Recursion`) sitting above the text box is pure visual bloat—it steals vertical space from your code editor and risks wiping out your pasted code if you accidentally click one.\n* **What I did:** I completely removed `Quick DSA Templates` and the extra input bar from [`app_build/index.html`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/index.html), [`app_build/app.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/app.js), and [`app_build/styles.css`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/styles.css).\n\nNow, when you click **`✏️ Paste / Edit Code`**, you get **only a clean, distraction-free code box**—paste your Python code, click **`▶ Run Code`**, and it visualizes immediately. Refresh your browser (`F5` / `Ctrl+R`) to see the clean editor."}
